OVERVIEW: Remove build setting from specified targets

Remove a build setting key from one or more targets.

Examples:
  xcodeproj-cli remove-build-setting SWIFT_VERSION --targets MyApp,MyTests
  xcodeproj-cli remove-build-setting CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY -t MyApp -c Debug

USAGE: xcodeproj-cli remove-build-setting [--project <project>] [--workspace <workspace>] [--verbose] [--dry-run] <key> --targets <targets> [--config <config>]

ARGUMENTS:
  <key>                   Build setting key to remove

OPTIONS:
  -p, --project <project> Path to .xcodeproj file (default: looks for
                          *.xcodeproj in current directory)
  -w, --workspace <workspace>
                          Path to .xcworkspace file
  -V, --verbose           Enable verbose output with performance metrics
  --dry-run               Preview changes without saving
  -t, --targets <targets> Comma-separated list of target names
  -c, --config <config>   Optional: specific configuration name
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

